# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_populate.py" "CO-CHANGE POPULATE GATE: PASS" "co-change populate (history -> stored signal, the piece that makes it appear in prod)" "co-change POPULATE: the glue that makes co-change actually APPEAR in production -- a repo's COMMIT HISTORY -> the stored, queryable co-change signal, end to end. The code graph is ingested from a TARBALL (a snapshot at one sha -- NO history), so the empirical coupling would never be populated without a separate history fetch; ingest.populate_cochange closes it with a BLOBLESS, NO-CHECKOUT clone (github_rest.history_clone: commit + tree metadata + paths, NEVER a file blob) -> the precision-disciplined extractor (giant-commit skip + support floor + LIFT) -> the gated write path. Proven on a real git history against a real scratch-tenant DB: (1) POPULATE end to end (clone dir -> cochange_pairs -> ingest_cochange -> co_change table -> the partner read surfaces the real coupling: editing auth surfaces api at confidence 5/7 + lift 5x); (2) NO-CHECKOUT sufficiency (the clone has .git but an EMPTY working tree -- co-change reads HISTORY, not bodies -- the content-free shape history_clone produces in prod); (3) CONTENT-FREE (the crafted repo's SECRET file bodies + commit messages never reach the stored/returned values); (4) FAIL-OPEN (a clone that FAILS reports ok:False content-free, never raises, populates nothing -- onboarding/the graph are never aborted by the advisory 2nd signal); (5) the 50-file giant commit mints no partners through the populate path. The installation token is injected via GIT_CONFIG_* env (http.extraHeader), never in the clone URL/argv (no ps/log leak)" "co-change populate: history -> blobless no-checkout clone -> extractor -> gated store -> queryable partner read; content-free, fail-open, no-checkout-sufficient, giant-commit-skip survives, token never in argv" 24
